hey at seven I believe that it's  important to thank the people in your  life who have helped make your life  exceptional and your business  exceptional because it's hard running  the company and we have to rely on other  people to help us out so I thought I  would create a regular series thanking  the people in my life and hopefully it  inspires you to thank and recognize the  people in yours as well let them know  that hey we appreciate all the work  you've done to help us get to where we  are so today this is a big one I want to  thank my parents now my parents have  always been super supportive of  everything that I've done in my career  even growing up all the things that I  wanted to do they are not entrepreneurs  themselves but they always supported my  business ideas I remember one of my  first ideas was to buy and sell baseball  cards I had a huge passion for baseball  and love going and buying cards and  selling amount of profit and I remember  maybe once a month going up to this  place called the orange tent that was  maybe two and a half three hours away  from my house and they would drive me  there and they would look around but the  main reason I went there was because  there was this store this little shop  set up within the orange tank where they  sold baseball cards and I would always  get excited forward and bring my money  and bring my cards and haggle and  negotiate and and you know I was maybe  ten years old and I would negotiate you  know down to the last nickel or dime and  it was it was my early days of  entrepreneurship but negotiation and my  parents had no idea about baseball cards  they didn't really care about baseball  cards but they saw that their son had a  passion for something and they were  extremely helpful and supportive in  helping me you know foster that and so  I'm really appreciative I remember  probably the hardest moment ever in my  business career was in my first real  company was a software company and you  know wasn't making the money wanted to  make barely surviving struggling to get  by having disagreements with my partners  and I remember one day in particular  where I was having a family dinner so is  at home and my pen  house and I got into an argument with my  business partner we had been struggling  for so long and we both had the same  goal born and see our company succeed we  just had different visions on how to do  it what to do next and I think when  you're just struggling and struggling  for so long you get frustrated and you  start to snap at each other and after  the call you know at the end of the call  I said like this is it I quit I don't  want to do this anymore this business is  is just taking too much of me and I  don't see how we're gonna make it and  and that's it like I can't do this  anymore I'm quitting and I felt like  such a failure after that you know like  I put all this work and effort into it  and and to hear me say that I quit felt  like such a such a failure such a down  moment in my life was like the lowest  I've ever been in my life and I hung up  the phone on my partner and I just  started crying like uncontrollably  crying like everything was going wrong  and I think my mom heard that I was  crying and she came up and she put her  hand on my shoulder and you know asked  what was wrong and four for 10-15  minutes I couldn't even say anything it  was just too overwhelming no so upset  and frustrated disappointed myself I  just cried and the tears are coming down  my face and she just had her hand on my  shoulder and was there for me and you  know after about 10 15 minutes is able  to muster up a few words and even though  she didn't say anything we didn't really  have a huge conversation that night  having her there and having that support  you know meant a lot to me and helped me  get through that that tough night and  and the next day I got up and went back  to work and that's part of being an  entrepreneur and everything I've done my  parents have been extremely supportive  and even the stuff I'm doing now you  know my mom's always listening on the  radio show and watching the videos and  it's getting you know very involved and  again even though it doesn't really  apply to the things that she's doing in  her life it you know they both want to  see their son basics  cessful and they want to have but as  much as possible so thank you both of  you for all of your help over the years  it's meant a lot and I'll never forget  it emotional so for those of you again  you know try to recognize the people in  your life who have had a tremendous  impact on your business on your life  because we can't do it alone running the  business is really hard we need to lean  on people to help us we have to have  people support us through the way if  it's you know financial or ideas or just  a shoulder to lean on I'm sure there are  people in your life had an impact so  thank them you know an email a  handwritten note video like this firing  time today to thank somebody in your  life who's had that impact and that  they'll feel great about it and you'll  feel good about it to thank you guys if  you liked this video you know the drill  thumbs up below and I'd love to hear  from you please leave a comment under  this video let me know who supported you  and your ventures and if you have a  question let me know to it be happy  times for you see you guys soon
 

